1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:01,824
Running a small business

2
00:00:01,824 --> 00:00:03,664
in Germany means paperwork,

3
00:00:03,664 --> 00:00:05,503
often in a second language:

4
00:00:05,503 --> 00:00:08,055
registration forms, invoices, receipts,

5
00:00:08,055 --> 00:00:11,200
tax returns, and letters from the Finanzamt.

6
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:14,224
So I built German Business Kit:

7
00:00:14,224 --> 00:00:16,594
seven open-source skills that turn Claude

8
00:00:16,594 --> 00:00:18,560
or Codex into a business assistant

9
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:20,699
for sole traders in Germany.

10
00:00:20,699 --> 00:00:21,856
No new app.

11
00:00:21,856 --> 00:00:24,920
You just ask, in English, German or Russian.

12
00:00:25,920 --> 00:00:27,869
It asks only for what's missing,

13
00:00:27,869 --> 00:00:29,493
prepares a readable draft,

14
00:00:29,493 --> 00:00:30,846
and saves your facts,

15
00:00:30,846 --> 00:00:32,145
documents and next steps

16
00:00:32,145 --> 00:00:33,823
in one private folder.

17
00:00:33,823 --> 00:00:36,800
So next month, it continues where you stopped.

18
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:40,457
For example, a translator in Berlin asks:

19
00:00:40,457 --> 00:00:42,406
Freiberufler or Gewerbe?

20
00:00:42,406 --> 00:00:44,413
The real answer names the law,

21
00:00:44,413 --> 00:00:46,008
the one registration needed

22
00:00:46,008 --> 00:00:47,661
and its deadline, with links

23
00:00:47,661 --> 00:00:50,200
to the official sources it opened.

24
00:00:51,800 --> 00:00:53,750
It covers the whole journey:

25
00:00:53,750 --> 00:00:55,396
starting out, invoices,

26
00:00:55,396 --> 00:00:57,286
receipts and bank matching,

27
00:00:57,286 --> 00:00:59,846
tax preparation and Finanzamt replies,

28
00:00:59,846 --> 00:01:03,320
choosing services, and later changes or closing.

29
00:01:04,320 --> 00:01:06,335
Here it is in the real apps.

30
00:01:06,335 --> 00:01:08,295
In Claude, you ask in your own words

31
00:01:08,295 --> 00:01:10,364
and get one small first step.

32
00:01:10,364 --> 00:01:12,596
In Codex, all seven skills are ready,

33
00:01:12,596 --> 00:01:14,720
and it answers in German, too.

34
00:01:15,720 --> 00:01:18,460
One rule shapes everything: it prepares,

35
00:01:18,460 --> 00:01:20,266
you decide and send.

36
00:01:20,266 --> 00:01:21,574
You sign in to ELSTER

37
00:01:21,574 --> 00:01:23,193
or your bank yourself,

38
00:01:23,193 --> 00:01:25,560
and you make the final click.

39
00:01:26,560 --> 00:01:29,797
It's an early preview, and AI help, not tax advice.

40
00:01:29,797 --> 00:01:32,063
The kit is open source on GitHub.

41
00:01:32,063 --> 00:01:33,898
Try it with a made-up example,

42
00:01:33,898 --> 00:01:35,840
and tell me what's missing.
